WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.640
What wins this matchup: a&nbsp;
$300 million roller coaster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:07.680
or a ride based on "The Cat&nbsp;
in the Hat?" The answer…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:13.600
could surprise you? But the real surprise is how&nbsp;
low The Incredible Hulk Coaster is on this list.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:19.840
The wait times for Storm Force Accelatron aren't&nbsp;
usually too bad, but that's only because people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:24.960
are spending their time doing other things. It's&nbsp;
not an awful experience. It's an acceptable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:30.000
family-friendly teacup-clone, even if it's a bit&nbsp;
more dizzying than it needs to be. But it doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.560
make for a memorable time, either, and while&nbsp;
you're waiting for it to end in your spinning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:38.960
seat with your chin in your palm, you'll have&nbsp;
plenty of time to think about all the better&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:43.840
X-Men rides that could have been. Don't waste&nbsp;
your time unless you've hit everything else first.

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:48.880
Pteranodon Flyers isn't a bad ride&nbsp;
in and of itself. The problem? The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:54.400
ride is simply too restrictive, as only two&nbsp;
riders can use Pteranodon Flyers at a time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:57.840
one in front of the other, and&nbsp;
one of them has to be a kid, too.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:03.840
This means, A) you have to have or be a kid to&nbsp;
begin with, B) riders can't sit next to each&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:09.440
other and experience Flyers together, and C)&nbsp;
larger families are separated for the duration&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:14.560
and have to wait for the rest of the group at&nbsp;
one of the three confusingly arranged exits.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:20.320
This also leads to childless park visitors&nbsp;
being unnecessarily turned away from the ride.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:22.960
There just wasn't quite enough&nbsp;
thought put into this one.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:25.440
"Your scientists were so preoccupied&nbsp;
with whether or not they could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:26.640
they didn't stop to think if they should."

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:32.480
On One Fish, Two Fish, Red Fish, Blue Fish,&nbsp;
riders can move their little cartoon fish&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:38.560
cars up and down as they swing around in a circle.&nbsp;
The views of Seuss Landing are colorful and fun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:42.160
but they can be a bit distracting. That's&nbsp;
because if you don't pay attention to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:47.120
ride's catchy jingle, which subtly tells you&nbsp;
when and how to move your car, there's a chance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:51.600
you'll get splashed with a little stream of&nbsp;
water. It's a memorable little mechanism,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:56.640
but we can also see how it'd be a reason for&nbsp;
parents to take their kids on other, dryer rides.

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:02.720
Kiddie coasters have a tendency to get overlooked.&nbsp;
But Flight of the Hippogriff, in the Wizarding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:06.960
World of Harry Potter section of Islands of&nbsp;
Adventure, might be worth a visit if you've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:12.800
got kids young enough to enjoy it. It takes you&nbsp;
through the Forbidden Forest, past Hagrid's hut,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:17.200
and up to Buckbeak, the titular magical&nbsp;
creature, before looping back around.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:22.720
The track is predictably tame, although there&nbsp;
are some mildly unexpected twists that can force&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:26.960
a smile out of you along the way, and the&nbsp;
views of Hogwarts castle are spectacular.

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:32.880
Space shot rides definitely aren't for everyone.&nbsp;
They're the ones where you get shot up to the top&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:38.080
of a tower and then dropped rapidly, usually in&nbsp;
controlled bursts broken up with air cushions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:43.600
for a stop-and-start thrill experience. Doctor&nbsp;
Doom's Fearfall is one of the better ones, thanks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:49.200
to a fun queue that gets you into the story. The&nbsp;
problem? You'd better love that queue, because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:54.440
this is a long wait for a very short ride, so&nbsp;
only check this one out if you have time to spare.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:03:00.560
The Caro-seuss-el is exactly what it sounds&nbsp;
like: a carousel ride where the horses have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:05.920
been swapped out for Dr. Seuss characters. It's&nbsp;
good, family-friendly fun with a relatively short&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:10.800
wait time and a catchy little jingle. And if you&nbsp;
push on the levers on the character's necks or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:15.440
pull on their reigns, you can animate them,&nbsp;
giving this one an extra little bit of fun.

00:03:16.716 --> 00:03:21.920
The Cat's iconic Hat towers above Seuss Landing&nbsp;
and can be fairly easily seen from adjacent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:26.800
areas of the park. The ride itself is certainly&nbsp;
well put together: it's a track that takes you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:32.400
through a dimly lit, twisting hallway filled with&nbsp;
iconic scenes from the classic children's book.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:36.880
There's the talking fish, Thing 1 and Thing&nbsp;
2, lots of crazy furniture to look at,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:40.800
and much more. And of course, the Cat&nbsp;
makes plenty of appearances throughout.

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:46.400
The main problem with the ride is that it's too&nbsp;
scary for small kids, and too boring for adults.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:50.160
But if you're the exact right age in&nbsp;
between, you might enjoy it a lot.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:56.240
Dudley Do-right's Ripsaw Falls ride isn't&nbsp;
an essential stop, but it can be a fun way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.240 --> 00:04:00.480
for the family to beat the muggy Florida&nbsp;
heat with laughs and a whole lot of water.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:06.240
The queue is fun, and the ride provides an&nbsp;
iconic, 75-foot plunge into the water below.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:11.840
The climax of the ride leaves nobody dry. Anyone&nbsp;
who doesn't feel like getting soaked can still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:15.760
have fun with the ride: you just have to&nbsp;
stand by and watch people get drenched,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:19.360
or you can pay a small fee and shoot&nbsp;
them yourself with water turrets.

00:04:19.834 --> 00:04:25.520
Poseidon's Fury is at least as much fun for the&nbsp;
theater kid playing the archaeologist tour guide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:30.080
as it is for the families experiencing it.&nbsp;
The idea is that the guide needs your help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:34.640
navigating the Temple of Poseidon, which&nbsp;
is under attack from an evil dark lord.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:39.200
There's a great mix of physical setpieces&nbsp;
that someone clearly had a blast building&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:42.720
and digital effects that bring it all&nbsp;
to life with the help of your animated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:47.360
thoroughly entertaining guide. There are spooky&nbsp;
moments, but nothing sudden or shocking that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:53.680
parents of young tykes need to concern themselves&nbsp;
with. As of January 2022 the ride is closed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:56.720
but there are reports that it will&nbsp;
open back up in the very near future.

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:02.960
There are raft rides and log flumes in just about&nbsp;
any major theme park, including several others at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:09.040
Universal Studios itself. But what sets Jurassic&nbsp;
Park River Adventure apart is something that, on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:16.000
paper, would make it sound rather lame: education.&nbsp;
You lazily cruise past massive, life-size&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:21.440
animatronic dinos while a narrator fills you in&nbsp;
on the details of the real thing. Think of it as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:26.080
a time traveling boat tour. And if you're not into&nbsp;
learning, no worries, there's also an enormous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:31.040
85-foot plunge at the end that will soak everyone&nbsp;
on the ride. It's the best of both worlds!

00:05:32.715 --> 00:05:37.840
High above the family-oriented fun of Seuss&nbsp;
Landing, you'll find the High in the Sky Seuss&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:43.280
Trolley Train Ride, which takes families through&nbsp;
Seuss-styled circus tents and houses, filled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:48.240
with all the weird, wacky, colorful creatures&nbsp;
and contraptions you'd expect in such places.

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:52.240
They could have easily put a ride like this&nbsp;
on the ground, but instead they elevated it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:57.360
so the outdoor stretches in between the ride&nbsp;
setpieces offer spectacular views. All in all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:01.600
it's a fun, silly, colorful, relaxing way&nbsp;
to spend a few minutes with the kids while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:04.080
everyone takes a breather and plans the next stop.

00:06:05.751 --> 00:06:10.400
Popeye &amp; Bluto's Bilge-Rat Barges is a great&nbsp;
way for families to beat the Florida heat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:16.480
and kill an hour or two. Just pile into a big,&nbsp;
circular float and drift downstream, past plenty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:22.240
of colorful setpieces, classic, old school Popeye&nbsp;
characters, and other parts of Toon Lagoon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:26.960
It probably won't be anyone's favorite ride,&nbsp;
but wait times are short and anyone willing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:32.400
to get a little wet will have fun. Plus, it's a&nbsp;
nice way to quickly explore a fun but neglected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:36.400
part of the park that you probably won't&nbsp;
be spending too much time in otherwise.

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:42.800
This is simply one of the best trackless theme&nbsp;
park rides in the world. Riders board a safari&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:48.480
truck and get taken on a perilous journey through&nbsp;
a spooky, dark Pacific island based on Peter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:55.280
Jackson's 2005 "King Kong" movie. The ride blends&nbsp;
digital and physical effects to magical levels.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.280 --> 00:07:01.760
There are bats, giant bugs, spooky caves, bones&nbsp;
everywhere, and a huge fight between Kong and a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:06.800
giant dinosaur that sends your car reeling and&nbsp;
crashing over cliffs. It's an unforgettable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:11.440
experience truly worthy of the flagship&nbsp;
status it's created for itself at the park.

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:16.880
This one's a bit weird, because it's only half&nbsp;
in Islands of Adventure. But that's the whole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:21.920
point. Hop on the iconic train from the Harry&nbsp;
Potter world there and ride it to the other,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:27.760
original half of Universal Studios, or vice versa.&nbsp;
It functions more like a shuttle than a ride.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:33.120
Even so, though, the experience is almost as cool&nbsp;
as the Hogsmeade and Diagon Alley park sections,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:37.840
which bookend it. That's because it's not&nbsp;
just decorated like the Express on the inside:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:41.680
you get a digital display on the windows&nbsp;
that makes it look like you're traveling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:46.160
through the Wizarding World we see in the&nbsp;
films. Just hold on to your chocolate frogs!

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:53.280
"Watch it! Aw, that’s rotten luck!"

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:58.400
The queue and the visible setpieces around&nbsp;
Jurassic Park's VelociCoaster are all about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:03.920
velociraptors, everyone's favorite dinosaurs&nbsp;
ever since "Jurassic Park" made them famous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:07.840
so there's plenty of those to see and&nbsp;
hear as you move through the line.

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:13.120
Eventually you'll get to the coaster, though, and&nbsp;
to say it makes the rather underwhelming queue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:19.120
experience worth it is an understatement. Prepare&nbsp;
for high speeds, killer loops and twists, and big,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:24.400
fast drops. It's as solid a roller coaster&nbsp;
as you're likely to find just about anywhere,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:28.320
and a must-ride for first timers to&nbsp;
Universal and repeat visitors alike.

00:08:28.901 --> 00:08:35.360
The Incredible Hulk coaster is perhaps the most&nbsp;
iconic Universal Studios ride there is. Luckily,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:39.440
it's also one of the first things you'll get&nbsp;
to do upon entering the park. Unsurprisingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:43.920
the wait is long, given how easy the&nbsp;
coaster is to reach and how popular it is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:48.320
but Universal pulled out all the stops to&nbsp;
deck out the queue with blaring lights,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:53.680
sirens and cool, comic-booky sci-fi gizmos, so&nbsp;
don't worry about getting bored on the way up.

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:58.480
And the ride itself is worth the wait.&nbsp;
Appropriately enough, it's a powerful, angry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:03.840
green beast that plunges you into epic drops and&nbsp;
launches you into loops and twists at thrilling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:09.680
speeds. We will say this, though: while the ride&nbsp;
isn't necessarily too extreme for most theme park&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:15.120
enthusiasts, it's definitely a good idea to grab&nbsp;
a bite to eat after you get off, and not before.

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:21.200
Towering over Islands of Adventure and&nbsp;
visible from several remote areas of the park&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:26.560
is Hogwarts itself: the iconic castle-school&nbsp;
from the Harry Potter films. It's a good thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:31.600
that it takes so long to get to, because it builds&nbsp;
anticipation throughout the day and keeps everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:36.720
in your group excited to get to the next place.&nbsp;
The recreated town of Hogsmeade is just below&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:41.760
and offers an incredible, immersive experience&nbsp;
for Harry Potter fans and everyone else alike.

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:47.680
But the Forbidden Journey is the real draw here:&nbsp;
a massive 4D flying adventure where you follow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:53.120
Harry himself on a dizzying, dazzling flight&nbsp;
through the school grounds and away from dragons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:58.160
and dementors. The wait time can be absolutely&nbsp;
excruciating, but thanks to the ride and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:03.840
chance to explore the castle, we've never heard of&nbsp;
anyone regretting this one of a kind experience.

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:06.560
It's hard to make a better, more thrilling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:11.760
more impressive 4D movie experience than&nbsp;
The Amazing Adventures of Spider-Man.

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:16.800
The queue is almost as memorable as the ride&nbsp;
itself, allowing you to check out the inside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:22.160
of The Daily Bugle, the iconic fictional newspaper&nbsp;
that Peter Parker worked at. That's where grumpy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:27.680
editor J. Jonah Jameson recruits the guests to&nbsp;
get the scoop on the latest supervillain attack.

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:32.560
The ride itself throws you into the thick of&nbsp;
it alongside Spidey in his fight against the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:38.400
Sinister Syndicate, led by Doctor Octopus. It&nbsp;
pulls out all the stops to make it seem real:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:42.400
lighting effects, wind blasts,&nbsp;
simulator movements, and more.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:45.600
And keep your eyes out for a&nbsp;
cameo by the great Stan Lee!

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:49.040
"They've even added me to the 3D adventure.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:54.000
But I'm not going to tell you where to find&nbsp;
me! You'll have to discover that on your own!"

00:10:54.720 --> 00:11:00.080
The best ride at Islands of Adventure is none&nbsp;
other than Hagrid's Magical Creatures Motorbike&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:05.840
Adventure, a $300 million behemoth&nbsp;
of a coaster that opened in 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:11.200
in which the titular character takes you through&nbsp;
a maze of epic Harry Potter setpieces filled with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:16.800
three-headed dogs, unicorns, and other magical&nbsp;
creatures that roam the woods around Hogwarts.

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:20.160
It's a good thing the ride is so&nbsp;
great, too — because when it opened,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:26.720
wait times often exceeded eight hours. The&nbsp;
massive hype for the ride set a brutally high bar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:30.240
but it's safe to say that the&nbsp;
coaster reached it and then some.

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:33.120
